ALGORITHM -
MaxMin(A, low, high)

If only one element:
    min = max = A[low]

If two elements:
    compare them
    smaller = minimum
    larger = maximum

Otherwise:
    divide array into two halves
    find MaxMin of left half
    find MaxMin of right half

    compare the two minimums
    compare the two maximums



Complexity
For n elements:
T(n)=2T(n/2)+2

Hence:
T(n)=O(n)

For even n, the number of comparisons is:
3n/2 −2

So the number of comparisons is bounded by:3N/2

which validates the requirement of the question.
